{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790354960,"nonce":"zf3/mZFeudD/O5JxOs9WnY7JkzA=","title":"Build macros in other modules were never registered; bodyless macro declarations aborted the scan; ordinary static builders and macro-time `macro class` unsupported","message":"- `@:build(unit.issues.misc.Issue6873Macro.build())` names a module the file never imports, so the module was never loaded and its macro was \"undefined\" (Issue6873, Issue12030).\n- A build macro's body ran with an empty import map, so its own `import haxe.macro.Context` did not resolve.\n- An ordinary (non-`macro`) static function used as a builder (Issue12030Macro.build) was not a registered macro.\n- `macro static function format(...):Expr;` with no body, the non-macro side of `#if macro`, failed the whole scan (Issue10012, Issue9928). The file's own macro-context view, where the body lives, was skipped as a dependency because it has the same filename.\n- MacroStringTools.formatString, Rest.toArray and macro-time `(macro class X {...}).fields` were missing.\n\nFix: the driver loads modules named in @:build/@:autoBuild; build bodies get their module's imports; an unregistered builder call is evaluated against the class registry; bodyless macro declarations are skipped and the file's own view is scanned; formatString parses its argument as a format string; `macro class` at macro time builds a TypeDefinition whose fields have the build-field shape.\n\nConformance 671 -\u003e 673 (Issue10012, Issue9928), 0 LOST. MOVED Issue12030 to WRONG_ANSWER: a function-local `static var` is re-initialised on every call (prints AA, want AB), a separate language gap. Issue6873 now needs ComplexTypeTools.toType and TypeTools.followWithAbstracts.","files":null}]}